Z||000000||speed1||07-09-2001||09:11 PM||||I need to drop my engine cradle and I have done before by jacking up the ass end with a floor jack.  I have access to a 4post lift and was thinking of supporting from front to the cradle mounts on the lift and leaving the ass end off the lift.  It would be like using a pad contact lift.  Has anyone tried this or I am the only crazy person to think of this? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Fiero||07-09-2001||10:24 PM||||Thats how they show it in the Haynes manual. They have the engine/cradle assembly on a pallet and then raise the car up and away from it and then roll out with a pallet jack.<P>Whew.....one long ass sentence. Dont see why it wouldnt work.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG"> <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"||||reg||1
